            <ArticleTitle>Painful palpitations: chest pain associated with postextrasystolic ST depression.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>358-61</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Postextrasystolic T-wave changes have been described as early as 1915. The significance and mechanism of such changes remain controversial. Because postextrasystolic ST changes are rare, much of the ensuing discussion concentrates on the closely related and more commonly reported phenomenon of postextrasystolic T-wave inversion. This report documents the case of a 67-year-old man with a history of coronary artery disease who was admitted to the hospital with chest pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
